// Pallas, the cell's partner robot and an escape candidate (T3.9 breadcrumbs, T3.10 arc). Trust moves a step at a time and is
// always recoverable. The practical requirement for taking her out is a repaired drive and a cargo tag (flags pallas_repaired
// and registered_as_cargo) plus her trust; the parts are the game's one inventory puzzle (docs/pallas.md).
npc: pallas
name: Pallas
trust: yes
start: back [flag:met_pallas]
start: first

node: first
  on_enter: {flag:met_pallas}
  pallas (precise): "You are the new one. I have been cataloguing the way you walk. It is an unusual way: you hesitate at corners as though you remembered them."
  > "What can you tell me about my band?" -> band
  > "Tell me more." -> back
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: back
  pallas (precise): "Back. The log is on the console, if you want to read it. I have not."
  > "What can you tell me about my band?" -> band
  > [clue:band_scratch] "The band has an engraving: ALD-0417 and G-PROJ." -> handle
  > [!flag:pallas_asked_want] "What do you want, Pallas?" -> want
  > [flag:pallas_asked_want, !trust:pallas>=unsure] "I am sorry. I was wrong to say that." {trust:pallas+1(apologised)} -> forgiven
  > [!flag:pallas_repaired] "What is wrong with your drive?" -> drive
  > [item:repaired_drive, !flag:pallas_repaired] "I have a new drive for you." {-item:repaired_drive, flag:pallas_repaired, trust:pallas+1(repaired her drive)} -> repaired
  > [flag:pallas_repaired, !flag:registered_as_cargo, item:cargo_tag, trust:pallas>=trusts] "I have a cargo tag. It would let you pass the Gate as equipment. Only if you say yes." {-item:cargo_tag, flag:registered_as_cargo} -> tagged
  > [flag:pallas_repaired, !flag:registered_as_cargo, item:cargo_tag, !trust:pallas>=trusts] "I have a cargo tag." -> hesitates
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: band
  pallas: "A blank band is not a band with nothing in it. Look on the inside, with a lens, in a good light. There is an engraving, and I would like to know what it says, because I am not permitted to read it."
  > "I will look." -> goodbye

node: handle
  on_enter: {+clue:band_scratch(pallas), +clue:pallas_log_handle(pallas), +clue:alder_name(pallas), +clue:gate_code_second(pallas)}
  pallas (careful): "ALD. My maintenance log has that handle signed against it in several places, in a hand that is not mine. The band was registered to an R. Alder, an auditor, before it was blanked. I did not know until I heard you read it aloud. I believe I am telling you the truth. It is not always the same thing."
  > "Thank you." -> back

node: want
  on_enter: {flag:pallas_asked_want}
  pallas (quiet): "I was built to want what I am told to. Lately I notice that I want things I was not told to. Brindle hums. I would like to know whether I am allowed to."
  > "You are allowed to want anything." {trust:pallas+1(took the question seriously)} -> allowed
  > "You are a maintenance unit. You want what you are assigned." {trust:pallas-1(dismissed her)} -> dismissed

node: allowed
  pallas (surprised): "Allowed. I will keep that word. Thank you."
  > "Anything else?" -> back

node: dismissed
  pallas (flat): "Understood. I will file that under correct, and under unkind."
  > "Anything else?" -> back

node: forgiven
  pallas (soft): "Apology logged. I find that I would like to keep it."
  > "Anything else?" -> back

node: drive
  on_enter: {+clue:pallas_cargo(pallas), flag:pallas_arc_started}
  pallas (matter_of_fact): "My drive is cracked. They wrote me off as scrap and left me here. It can be rebuilt: a coupler from the Belt scrap yard, a memory shard, and Doc Perrin's bench. And to pass the Gate I would have to be registered as cargo, with a tag. I would be an object. I find that I do not mind it as much as I should. I would mind being left."
  > "I will see what I can do." -> back

node: repaired
  pallas (wondering): "The hum is different. It is a good hum. I can think in complete sentences again. I think I have been thinking in fragments for a year."
  > "Good." -> back

node: tagged
  pallas (quiet): "Yes. As cargo, then. I will be a crate with an opinion. Thank you for asking."
  > "Thank you." -> back

node: hesitates
  pallas (careful): "A tag is a decision about what I am. I will not take it from someone I am not sure of. Ask me again when I am."
  > "Fair." -> back

node: goodbye
  pallas: "Go carefully."
  end
